.','A2':'Master calls BeTheLeader after selected leader failure; per-instance ballot handling supplies request qualification.'},unknowns=['Even-membership admissibility and intended fast-quorum sizing are not explicitly documented in read sources.'])\nbehavior('B-persist','A6','recordInstanceMetadata, recordCommands and sync',['S-store','S-base','S-config'],writes=['Durable guard otherwise no-op; metadata writes bal then overwrites same four bytes with vbal, followed by Status, Seq, Deps. Base StableStore is nil; launcher uses Durable=false.'],cross_activity_effects={'A2':'Any promise reconstruction would depend on a separate supported store initialization and decoding path.'},unknowns=['No captured restart decoder or initialized store found by StableStore search; durable-mode responsibility remains unresolved.'])\nbehavior('B-client','A7','PROPOSE received on client connection',['S-client','S-preaccept','S-base'],execution_owner='Replica client listener then run goroutine',protocol_context='Client CommandId/Timestamp and locally assigned instance',external_effects=['LRead=false in EPaxos initialization routes ordinary commands to delayed proposal channel; handlePropose batches available commands. Dreply defaults true.'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Proposal batch becomes commands for a new instance in local row.'},unknowns=['Client retry handling is explicitly TODO in handlePropose; no exactly-once responsibility is presumed.'])\nF=[dict(id='F-record',meaning='The local instance record carries current promised ballot bal, value ballot vbal, phase Status, commands and ordering attributes used in protocol replies and recovery selection; fields are not asserted to advance atomically or to certify acceptance.',identity={'replica':'origin replica row','instance':'instance index','observer':'replica holding the local record'},validity_context='In-memory record at one replica in fixed membership; bal and vbal may differ after Prepare and status may remain unchanged after Accept.',representation=['Instance.bal','Instance.vbal','Instance.Status','Instance.Cmds','Instance.Seq','Instance.Deps'],durability='In-memory in launcher configuration; guarded persistence does not establish restart reconstruction.',recovery='Prepare reports the record; recovery selection uses value ballot and status before Accept or restarted phase1.',source_ids=['S-preaccept','S-accept','S-recovery','S-commit'],unknowns=['Which acknowledged value information remains recoverable after an acceptor retains preaccepted status?']),dict(id='F-decision',meaning='A local instance is marked COMMITTED with its command and ordering attributes; execution additionally requires commands and ready dependency records.',identity={'replica':'origin row','instance':'instance index','observer':'local replica'},validity_context='Fast/slow leader decision, received Commit, or recovery installation of committed history; local status can later become EXECUTED.',representation=['Instance.Status','Instance.Cmds','Instance.Seq','Instance.Deps'],durability='Volatile in default launcher configuration.',recovery='Recovery can install selected committed/executed record; Commit can be rejected below local promised ballot.',source_ids=['S-preaccept','S-accept','S-commit','S-recovery','S-exec'])]\nroles=json.load(open('../research.json'))['activity_roles']\nactivities=[dict(class_id=a,applicability='applicable',purpose=r['relation'],realization_summary={'A1':'Per-instance preaccept/accept quorum formation and commit delivery.','A2':'Per-instance ballot qualification plus recovery proposer bookkeeping.','A3':'Execution-triggered Prepare recovery and status-dependent restart.','A4':'Master registration and fixed peer list with Alive transport state.','A5':'Dependency SCC execution and key-value state.','A6':'Volatile history plus optional incomplete persistence surface; restart contract unknown.','A7':'Proposal batching and deferred execution replies.'}[a],source_ids={'A1':['S-preaccept','S-accept'],'A2':['S-ballot','S-recovery'],'A3':['S-loop','S-recovery'],'A4':['S-master','S-base'],'A5':['S-exec'],'A6':['S-store','S-config'],'A7':['S-client','S-exec']}[a]) for a,r in roles.items()]\ndef path(text,bs,fs,ss):return dict(explanation=text,behavior_ids=bs,fact_ids=fs,source_ids=ss)\nm=dict(version=1,target_profile=dict(system_boundary='Captured Go EPaxos package and in-repository replica, master, client, state and launcher support. Other protocol implementations excluded.',protocol_contexts=['Fixed membership','Per-origin instance rows','Crash/delay investigation under configured failure count; Byzantine inputs not assumed'],external_interfaces=['Client PROPOSE stream','Peer serialized RPCs','Master registration and BeTheLeader RPC'],variants=['Thrifty=true forced by EPaxos constructor','Launcher Durable=false, transconf=false, batchWait=0','Exec=\"'!Noop; Dreply=true'\"'],source_ids=['S-init','S-config','S-client','S-transport']),activities=activities,behaviors=B,facts=F,surfaces=[dict(entry_point='recordInstanceMetadata',disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['B-persist'],reason='Does any supported durable/restart use require retaining both bal and vbal despite overlapping bytes?',source_ids=['S-store'],high_consequence=True),dict(entry_point='Replica.FastQuorumSize',disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['B-membership'],reason='Determine whether F+(F+1)/2 is sufficient for implemented formation/recovery intersection, using actual supported configurations.',source_ids=['S-base','S-config'],high_consequence=True),dict(entry_point='updateAttributes',disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['B-phase1'],reason='Exact-key conflict index differs from state.Conflict range-scan semantics; investigate scan applicability and ordered execution responsibility.',source_ids=['S-attrs','S-state'],high_consequence=True)],core_overview=dict(status='usable',formation=path('A client proposal allocates its origin row slot and establishes command/Seq/Deps at its owner. PreAccept receivers qualify ballot and merge local conflicts, reporting current value ballot and status. Matching replies supply the fast threshold; initial ballot plus equality and large-N committed-dependency conditions permit direct commit, otherwise Accept is broadcast and matching majority replies commit. Commit propagates the full tuple. Execution waits for committed dependency graph and orders SCCs before application and default client response.',['B-client','B-phase1','B-accept','B-commit','B-execute'],['F-record','F-decision'],['S-client','S-preaccept','S-accept','S-send','S-exec']),context=path('Authority is per instance, not solely the master-selected leader. Initial ballot equals origin replica; recovery replaces leader bookkeeping and chooses a ballot based on proposer id and, when IsLeader, maxRecvBallot. Prepare raises the local promise and returns prior value ballot/status; formation rejects older requests and reply handlers qualify lastTriedBallot/phase. Execution detects incomplete work and queues recovery. Prepare quorum selection adopts highest value-ballot record and chooses committed installation, Accept, or restarted phase1; old client proposals are retained. Already committed records resist subsequent Accept and Commit replacement.',['B-authority','B-recover-select','B-membership'],['F-record','F-decision'],['S-ballot','S-recovery','S-master','S-accept','S-commit','S-loop']),connection=path('Formation writes the same tuple and status that Prepare exposes to new owners. bal qualifies old requests while vbal and Status determine how old support is interpreted during recovery. Acks can contribute to local commit even though the receiver Accept path does not change Status; this discrepancy is retained rather than assuming an acceptance guarantee. Commit and execution establish prior decisions that restrict later handlers. Per-message delay goroutines mean pending messages can overlap authority changes; no FIFO handler-delivery assumption is used.',['B-phase1','B-accept','B-authority','B-recover-select','B-commit','B-execute'],['F-record','F-decision'],['S-accept','S-recovery','S-transport','S-commit']),open_details=['Legal recovery histories for missing ACCEPTED status and changed local value ballot.','Quorum-size applicability across N; duplicate reply support assumptions.','SCAN conflict coverage, SCC tie-break reachability and optional persistence obligations.'],core_gaps=[],rationale='Both core relationships and their connection have been traced through source, including fixed membership, network dispatch, recovery and consumption. Local discrepancies remain questions, not asserted defects.'))\nq=dict(question='After a nonstale Accept is acknowledged, can recovery reliably distinguish and preserve its accepted tuple when handleAccept leaves Status unchanged?',importance='If acknowledged accepted support is reinterpreted as preaccepted or absent, a later owner may select inconsistent ordering attributes or commands, threatening per-instance agreement. This is a potential consequence, not an observed violation.',source_ids=['S-accept','S-recovery','S-preaccept','S-types'],participants=['Initial instance owner','Accept receiver','Recovery owner and Prepare quorum'],objects=['Instance record and PrepareReply'],contexts=['Fixed membership and constructor-enforced thriftiness','Crash-stop and delayed messages; no arbitrary duplicate RPC injection'],event_paths=['startPhase1 -> PreAcceptReply -> bcastAccept -> handleAccept -> handlePrepare -> handlePrepareReply'],activity_classes=['A1','A2','A3'],behavior_ids=['B-accept','B-authority','B-recover-select'],fact_ids=['F-record'],supporting_behavior_ids={'B-phase1':'Produces the proposal and slow-path Accept preceding the investigated acknowledgement.','B-membership':'Defines quorum sizes and transport delivery constraints.','B-execute':'Queues recovery for incomplete instances.'},obligation_relation_kind='recovery',counterevidence=['Accept updates both ballot fields and ordering attributes; absence of a status update alone does not prove information loss.','Prepare returns commands and attributes in addition to Status; highest-value-ballot selection may preserve the same tuple.','Commit delivery and already-committed guards may prevent divergence in histories where a decision was propagated.'],unknowns=['Which legal crash/delay history exposes the status distinction after a completed slow-path acknowledgement?','Does a sourced local acceptance/recovery responsibility suffice, or is a same-history divergence needed to establish the intended guarantee?'],priority=3,trigger_rationale='The receiver records Accept attributes without recording ACCEPTED, while the directly downstream recovery switch explicitly assigns accepted and preaccepted records different continuation paths. Source and a small controlled history can discriminate this; a costly cluster-wide test is premature. Persistence is lower priority because default durability is disabled; quorum sizing is retained as another relationship.',disposition='concrete_suspicion',preferred_check='controlled_schedule')\njson.dump(m,open('initial-map.json','w'),indent=2)\njson.dump(dict(action='continue',rationale='Record the two core relationships and select the sourced Accept-to-recovery status discrepancy for legal-history investigation.',sources=sources,map_path='initial-map.json',question=q),open('submission.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\npython3 build_initial.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
